ited guests will introduce students to resources and opportunities for research, internships, and study abroad as well as community-engaged learning. In addition, the course outlines strategies for a successful academic trajectory and creates opportunities for students to forge connections with peers in their major as well as across majors in the College of Human Ecology.", "catalogBreadth": "", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": ["Understand the mission and learning outcomes of the College of Human Ecology and the majors in the College.", "Be familiar with resources that support academic success and allow exploration of co-curricular experiences, such as study abroad, internships, community-engaged learning, and research, and how to locate these resources.", "Draft a tentative four-year plan including course planning and strategy for including desired experiences potentially including research, study abroad, internships, competitions, community-engaged learning, and other growth experiences."], "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "HE", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}, {"strm": 2853, "crseId": 350003, "crseOfferNbr": 1, "subject": "HE", "catalogNbr": "1115", "titleShort": "Critical Reading & Thinking", "titleLong": "Critical Reading and Thinking", "crseAttrs": [], "crseAttrValueGroups": [], "enrollGroups": [{"classSections": [{"ssrComponent": "LEC", "ssrComponentLong": "Lecture", "section": "001", "classNbr": 8307, "meetings": [{"classMtgNbr": 1, "timeStart": "11:15AM", "timeEnd": "12:05PM", "startDt": "08/21/2023", "endDt": "12/04/2023", "instructors": [{"instrAssignSeq": 1, "netid": "msc7", "firstName": "Mike", "mid